  "body": "## Problem and decision\n\nThe owner directed the retained PostgreSQL/SQLite native implementation to C++ while preserving the merged C# API, C ABI, twelve package identities, stored data and behavior.\n\nFollowing Plan PR26, this change records C++20 runtime query metadata, direct libpq asynchronous PostgreSQL execution and sqlite3 prepared statements, bounded ownership, and LLVM Clang 23.1.5 conventions for the three intended platforms. Actual acceptance is Linux x64 only. The selected dependencies, source-level comparisons, configuration patch and notices are documented; reference frameworks are not added to the product closure.\n\nThe overlay binds the first published implementation checkpoint in product PR21 (`b383c130903daba059c364ff0615d80798da1a3f`, tree `4bd509e639f9779092f5d037c7690a57cf8a28d4`) and its dependency-lock SHA-256. Plan owns subsequent fixes, actual runtime evidence and final acceptance. This Design PR does not declare the product migration complete.\n\nHistorical accepted scope/contracts, public API inputs and verifier bytes remain unchanged. The new document gate invokes the original DB-Scope-01 gate at its immutable commit.\n\n## Validation and review\n\n- Current decision/identity/link/historical-byte verifier passed locally and independently.\n- Original DB-Scope-01 gate at `8298dc4` passed, including eight rejection controls.\n- Exact-head current design CI: https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave-Design/actions/runs/44956346986 — success.\n- Exact-head historical acceptance CI: https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave-Design/actions/runs/44956346889 — success.\n- Independent technical review checked the product Git tree and dependency-lock bytes, scope boundaries and absence of an unsupported product-acceptance claim.\n- `git diff --check` passed. No public release or Windows/macOS acceptance is asserted.",
